<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-24. SYSTEM FIELD. Marks the submission the SCORING model picked, as
        distinct from Is_Preferred_Broker__c (a human's manual appointment). Both flags can be
        true on DIFFERENT rows of the same Disposition at once: it is normal for the scored
        winner and the preferred broker to both carry Submission_Status__c = 'Selected'
        simultaneously. This flag is what tells the two "Selected" rows apart, and it becomes
        the field the exclusivity guard counts when validating that at most one row per flag
        type holds the Selected status for a given Disposition.

        WHAT WRITES IT: BovAutoSelectionService ONLY. No user, form, or data load should ever
        set this field.

        WHAT READS IT: BovAutoSelectionService's own exclusivity guard, and any future
        comparison/matrix logic that needs to distinguish a scored pick from a manual
        appointment among rows sharing Submission_Status__c = 'Selected'.

        FLS: READ ONLY in BOTH DPEG_Disposition_Edit and DPEG_Disposition_View, mirroring
        Is_Manually_Appointed__c's grant shape and reasoning — a user who could hand-edit this
        could corrupt which broker the approval routes to. Do NOT grant editable=true on either
        set for any persona.
    -->
    <fullName>Is_System_Selected__c</fullName>
    <defaultValue>false</defaultValue>
    <description>SYSTEM FIELD. Set only by BovAutoSelectionService. Marks the submission the scoring model picked, as distinct from Is_Preferred_Broker__c which marks a human-appointed submission. Read-only FLS everywhere by design.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>System-set by the scoring/auto-selection engine. Never edit by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>System Selected</label>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Checkbox</type>
</CustomField>
